From e2f023abd7283e2995b6805a31fc193c7d9598eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:48:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] KVM: arm64: Initialize all MTE tags in hugetlb folios

PG_mte_tagged is folio-wide for hugetlb, but sanitise_mte_tags() clears
only mapping_size bytes before publishing it. Dirty logging forces
mapping_size to PAGE_SIZE, and alignment or nested-stage constraints can
also select a base-page mapping within a multi-page hugetlb folio.

Publishing the flag after that partial clear makes untouched subpages
appear initialized and can expose stale allocation tags to the guest. Use
the whole-folio helper before publishing the flag, regardless of the
stage-2 mapping granule.

Fixes: 25c17c4b55de ("hugetlb: arm64: add mte support")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
index 9ba86450fe4af..364b159d3eda4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -1514,8 +1514,7 @@ static void sanitise_mte_tags(struct kvm *kvm, kvm_pfn_t pfn,
 	if (folio_test_hugetlb(folio)) {
 		/* Hugetlb has MTE flags set on head page only */
 		if (folio_try_hugetlb_mte_tagging(folio)) {
-			for (i = 0; i < nr_pages; i++, page++)
-				mte_clear_page_tags(page_address(page));
+			mte_clear_hugetlb_tags(folio);
 			folio_set_hugetlb_mte_tagged(folio);
 		}
 		return;
